<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ya'la ibn Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 958</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Ya'la ibn Muhammad al-Ifrani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ya'la ibn Muhammad al-Ifrani was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-ifran">Banu Ifran</a> Zenata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> of the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>. Allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a>, he founded the town of Ifgan and was killed in 958 during the western campaign of the Fatimid general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawhar-al-siqilli">Jawhar</a>.</p></div>
